      {
        "locale": "quz",
        "key": "formats22_page_preview",
        "english": "Selected page preview",
        "proposed_value": "Aqllasqa raphipa qhawanapaqraq siq\\'in",
        "decision": "accept",
        "final_value": "Aqllasqa raphipa qhawanapaqraq siq\\'in",
        "confidence": "moderate independent model whole-phrase review, not native-human certification",
        "whole_phrase_reasoning": [
          "Aqlla-sqa modifies raphi as selected, not a selection imperative. Raphi-pa marks the selected page as genitive possessor. The head siq’i-n is image plus third-person possessive matching that possessor; it is not the accusative form siq’i-ta used in the unavailable sentence.",
          "Qhawa-na-paq-raq modifies the image as for preliminary viewing. Together the phrase denotes the preliminary-view image of the selected page. This is context-dependent descriptive preview terminology, not a claim that -raq alone means software preview.",
          "The complete singular possessive noun phrase fits the ImageView accessible description. It neither commands selection/opening nor announces successful loading or final import. The explicit image noun is supported by the visual consumer.",
          "Longer than the English but structurally coherent. Acceptance rests on the full modifier/possessor/possessed-head structure, not automatic extension of accepted navigation words or lexical token matches."
        ],
        "consumer_semantics": "PDF/TIFF showPages ImageView accessible name, not ICO or generic web pages. Description names the role while the image is cleared or loading/error status appears separately. Only the alive/current-generation preview result installs a bitmap; no success or permanence is promised.",
        "format_checks": {
