      {
        "locale": "wo",
        "key": "ui_magnified_preview_ea9209",
        "english": "Magnified preview",
        "proposed_value": "Wonendi bi ñu màggal",
        "decision": "accept",
        "final_value": "Wonendi bi ñu màggal",
        "backtranslation": "The preview that is enlarged",
        "whole_phrase_reasoning": "Wonendi names the preliminary visual display. The b-class relative linker bi with the non-specific plural agent ñu and transitive enlargement verb màggal produces a descriptive relative clause, naturally read here as the preview which is enlarged. It is not an imperative to enable a feature and does not say the document dimensions have been enlarged. Relative-clause phrasing fits a dialog title for magnifier controls; it need not assert that the toggle is currently enabled. The nominal phrase is complete without an explicit copula or ellipsis. I accept the phrase as original Wolof composition at moderate model confidence, not as a source-attested whole phrase.",
        "confidence": "moderate independent whole-phrase model review",
        "runtime_assessment": "Title is selected only for showDrawingSettings(preview=true), whose controls toggle activeMagnifier and set previewMagnification. Renderer clips the preview lens and applies display scaling to the existing bitmap. Thus magnification concerns viewing, not a resampling/save operation or cursor-paint toggle. No success/permanence claim added.",
        "terminology_consistency": "Wonendi agrees with existing page-preview/error wording. The same-dialog toggle retains Seenu/seenub wording; this existing variation is explicitly left intact and is not certified as terminology uniformity. Synonymous preview wording does not change the proposed title’s function. Existing quoted toggle phrase is not a donor sentence or proof of grammar.",
